    "text": "{\n  \"anomaly_detected\": true,\n  \"confidence\": 0.4,\n  \"anomalies\": [\n    {\n      \"category\": \"open_connection\",\n      \"components\": [\"C4\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"C4.2\", \"U_MIC26903 (REG1).20 BST\", \"U_MIC26903 (REG1).9-12, 29 SW\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"REG_BST\", \"REG_SW\", \"GND\"],\n      \"observed\": \"On the Power sheet, the 2u2 bootstrap capacitor C4 has its top end on the REG_BST node (the D1 diode / BST line) and its bottom end on a GND symbol. The bootstrap capacitor is not drawn between BST and SW (REG_SW).\",\n      \"expected\": \"The bootstrap capacitor of the MIC26903 should connect between BST (pin 20) and SW (pins 9-12, 29), with the bootstrap diode feeding BST from the 5 V rail. Returning it to GND prevents the high-side gate drive from being generated.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"C4 2u2 with GND symbol at bottom, top on REG_BST node next to D1 SD103AWS (Power sheet, page 1)\"},\n        {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"REG1 MIC26903YJL-TR pin 20 BST labelled REG_BST (Power sheet, page 1)\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The high-side switch of the 5 V buck cannot be driven correctly, so the 5 V rail would fail to regulate or would not start, which in turn would break the 3V3 LDO and everything powered from it.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.4\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"bridged_nets\",\n      \"components\": [\"R3\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"R3.1\", \"R3.2\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"REG_BST\", \"REG_PG\"],\n      \"observed\": \"The 10k resistor R3 is wired between the bootstrap node (the C4 / D1 / REG_BST junction) and the REG_PG net, which is the MIC26903 power-good output (pin 25 PG). No 3V3 or 5V pull-up rail is shown on this resistor.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The open-drain PG output should be pulled up to a logic rail (for example +3.3V or the 5 V rail), not to the bootstrap node, which sits at a different voltage.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"R3 10k in series between the BST junction and the REG_PG label (Power sheet, page 1)\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"3.3 V rail: An LD39200PU33R LDO, fed from the 5 V rail, produces 3V3 for \\\"MCUs and Sensors\\\"\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The power-good signal is pulled to a bootstrap voltage instead of a logic level, so PG readings would be unreliable or would stress the pin.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.25\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The bootstrap capacitor C4 on the MIC26903 buck appears to return to GND rather than to SW, and the PG pull-up R3 appears to sit on the BST node, which would stop the 5 V regulator from working correctly. Confidence is moderate because the drawing is dense and the node connections near C4 and R3 are hard to trace precisely.\"\n}",
